Chemistry is the geometry of bonding relationships between atomic and molecular substructures. Atomic orbitals are stable attractors. Chemical bonding is a tensor bond between electron-density regions. Reaction pathways are gradient flows between attractor basins. Equilibrium is a stable attractor reached by free-energy minimization.

A molecule is not just a set of atoms; it is a resonance lattice of electron-density interactions with stable field configurations. Catalysis is the reshaping of the reaction landscape so that the system reaches a lower-energy path more efficiently.

